<title>BRAZIL: SOCCER-SOUTH AMERICAN CLUB RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-SOUTH AMERICAN CLUB RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of Wednesday's</p>
<p>matches in the first round of the South American Supercup.</p>
<p>In Buenos Aires: Boca Juniors (Argentina) 3 Argentinos</p>
<p>Juniors (Argentina) 0 (halftime 0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Silvio Carrario (61st minute), Gabriel Cedres</p>
<p>(69th), Sergio Martinez (86th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 4,100</p>
<p>Note: Boca and Argentinos are in a three-team group that</p>
<p>also includes Racing Club (Argentina). The winners qualify for</p>
<p>the second round. All other first round ties feature two teams</p>
<p>playing on a home-and-away basis.</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate under played, won, drawn, lost, goals</p>
<p>for, goals againsts, points)</p>
<p> Boca Juniors		3  2  1  0  6  1  7</p>
<p> Racing Club		 3  1  2  0  3  1  5</p>
<p> Argentinos Juniors	4  0  1  3  0  7  0</p>
<p>First round, second leg</p>
<p>In Brasilia: Flamengo (Brazil) 1 Independiente (Argentina) 0</p>
<p>(1-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Fabio Baiano (39th)</p>
<p>Attendance; 19, 172</p>
<p>Flamengo win 1-0 on aggregate</p>
<p>The Supercup is played every year between past winners of</p>
<p>the Libertadores Cup.</p>
<p>Played Tuesday:</p>
<p>South American Conmebol Cup, first round, first leg</p>
<p>In Braganca Paulista, Brazil: Bragantino (Brazil) 5</p>
<p>Palmeiras (Brazil) 1 (2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Bragantino - Kelly (21st, penalty, and 66th) Sandro, own</p>
<p>goal (39th), Alex (63rd), Gilson (90th)</p>
<p>Palmeiras - Luizao (50th, penalty)</p>
